    ["developer_files",
    ".CAR",
    "Compiled Asset Catalog",
    "3.9",
    "Data file used by Car Explorer, a program designed for viewing information about different car models; saved in the eXtensible Car Description (XCD) format, a standardized specification for storing automobile data; includes information such as make and model, year, price, physical dimensions, and related images. By design, CAR files store information about all models for one make (or company) from a single year. Car files are often distributed as collections, or an archive that contains multiple CAR files in a compressed format. NOTE: The Car Explorer application is no longer available. Windows Car Explorer. A CAR file is a Component Application Resource used by applications developed for the Brew Mobile Platform (MP). It describes assets available to an executing application. CAR files are compiled into binary.BAR files that are loaded when an application is run. Application resources in the older BREW 3.x and 4.x development programs use the.BRX extension. However, BRX files have been deprecated with the release of Brew MP. You can convert BRX files to CAR files using the Brew MP SDK. NOTE: The Brew MP SDK is a suite of programs and plug-ins. For example, the SDK includes Brew MP development plug-ins for Microsoft Visual Studio, Adobe Flash, and Eclipse. Windows Qualcomm Brew MP SDK Mac Qualcomm Brew MP SDK Linux Qualcomm Brew MP SDK. A CAR file is a compressed archive created by the CAR compression utility. It contains files used by SAPs enterprise resource planning (ERP) software. Often, CAR files contain SAP executables. CAR is a compression utility included with versions 4.6B and below of SAP. It can be used to compress one or more files into a CAR archive, for easier delivery to end-users. Users can then decompress the archive using CAR on their system. In version 4.6C, SAP overhauled the CAR utility and renamed it to SAPCAR. SAPCAR produces archives that use the.SAR extension. However, SAPCAR can still decompress and extract files from CAR archives. You can extract the files a CAR archive contains using the CAR or SAPCAR utilities (Windows, Linux). Windows SAP CAR. SAP SAPCAR. Linux SAP CAR. SAP SAPCAR. File created by Gary Gadget: Building Cars, a childrens game that allows users to design, build, and drive cars; contains car part numbers for the user-built saved car; includes any medals won with the car. NOTE: CAR files are located in the Autos folder of the games directory. Unfortunately, the Viva Media Gary Gadget: Building Cars program is no longer available for download. Windows Viva Media Gary Gadget: Building Cars Mac Viva Media Gary Gadget: Building Cars. A CAR file is a compiled asset catalog created by Apple Xcode to store assets, such as icons, images, and textures, for iOS, tvOS, watchOS, and macOS applications. App developers compile CAR files from.xcassets folders to distribute with the app bundle. Apple developed the proprietary CAR format to efficiently package assets at different resolutions for apps. CAR file open in Asset Catalog Tinkerer 2 Apple introduced the CAR format in September 2013 when it released Xcode 5 and iOS 7. When developers build an iOS, tvOS, watchOS, or macOS application in Xcode, they place the apps assets in an Assets.xcassets folder and then compile it to the CAR format to distribute with the app bundle. Typically, you can find the CAR file packaged with an app in its Resources directory. For example, you can navigate to the CAR file packaged with iMovie in macOS by following these steps: Right-click the iMovie app (.APP file) in the Applications directory and and select Show Package Contents to open it as a macOS package. Double-click Contents, then open the Resources folder. Navigate to the Assets.car file. NOTE: Apple continuously develops the CAR format, adding new features with each version. Assets.car - Name of the CAR file packaged in the Resources directory of an application installation. CAR files are not intended to be opened. Instead, they are packaged with an app to store assets used by the app. However, if you are looking to extract or modify an asset, such as an icon or texture, you can open a CAR file with various Mac programs, including Asset Catalog Tinkerer, ThemeEngine, iOS Asset Extractor, and acextract. For example, to open a CAR file with Asset Catalog Tinkerer, select File → Open. NOTE: While Apple Xcode creates CAR files, it cannot open them. Several applications, including Asset Catalog Tinkerer and Pragmatic Code Crunch, can extract assets from CAR files and convert them to other formats. For example, Asset Catalog Tinkerer can convert the assets stored in a CAR file to PNG images. To convert all of the assets in a CAR file with Asset Catalog Tinkerer, select File → Export All Images. Additionally, to convert a specific asset with Asset Catalog Tinkerer, select File → Export Selected Images. Mac Asset Catalog Tinkerer. Pragmatic Code Crunch. ThemeEngine. iOS Asset Extractor. acextractFree.",
    "Windows Car Explorer. Windows Qualcomm Brew MP SDK. Mac Qualcomm Brew MP SDK. Linux Qualcomm Brew MP SDK. Windows SAP CAR. SAP SAPCAR. Linux SAP CAR. SAP SAPCAR. Windows Viva Media Gary Gadget: Building Cars. Mac Viva Media Gary Gadget: Building Cars. Mac Asset Catalog Tinkerer. Pragmatic Code Crunch. ThemeEngine. iOS Asset Extractor. acextract.",
    "?"],
    ["developer_files",
    ".BET",
    "BETA Source File",
    "3.9",
    "Program file containing source code written in BETA, a modern object-oriented programming language; based off of Simula and developed within the Scandinavian School of object-orientation. BETA includes powerful data abstraction features that allow programmers to easily design programs. The language structure also enables reusability of program designs and implementations. BETA programs can be compiled using the BETA compiler, included with the Mjolner System development software package. Windows Edit with a text editor Compile with a BETA Compiler Mac Edit with a text editor Compile with a BETA Compiler Linux Edit with a text editor Compile with a BETA Compiler.",
    "Windows Edit with a text editor Compile with a BETA Compiler. Mac Edit with a text editor Compile with a BETA Compiler. Linux Edit with a text editor Compile with a BETA Compiler.",
    "?"],
    ["developer_files",
    ".FRM",
    "Visual Basic Text Form",
    "3.9",
    "An FRM file contains a form that may have been created by a variety of programs, such as Microsoft Visual Studio or Adobe FrameMaker. It is typically used to define fields within tables and it may also store database data, depending on the format. Windows Microsoft Visual Studio 2022. Corel WordPerfect 2021. Adobe FrameMaker. DataCAD. A FRM file contains the formatting information or structure data for a table in a MySQL database. It specifies the table stored in the database and defines the fields and structure of the table. FRM files are generated when a MySQL table is created and they bear the same name as the tables for which they store the formatting information. You will most likely only encounter MySQL FRM files if you are a database architect or developer configuring the MySQL data storage backend of an application. The files are created in the same directory that represents the database to which the tables they are storing formatting information for belong. FRM files are not meant to be manually opened. Instead, they are referenced by MySQL to format each table in a database. FRM files are saved along with an.MYD file, which contains the actual data stored in the database. Both files are necessary for MySQL to recognize the database. If the MySQL database uses MyISAM tables, an.MYI file is also used and required. There are some instances when data in a MySQL database is lost or becomes corrupt. Utilities like Aryson MySQL Database Repair may be used to recover or repair the FRM files that store the lost formatting information. NOTE: FRM is short for FoRMat.. Windows MySQL. Aryson MySQL Database Repair. Mac MySQL. Linux MySQL. Stores the text information for a Visual Basic form; used to save forms created in a Visual Basic project during the development of a program. Windows Microsoft Visual Basic 6. Microsoft Visual Studio 2022. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Other text editor. Form created by AccountEdge Pro, a business accounting application; contains data in a customized layout for checks, paychecks, receipts, payment notifications, invoices, statements, purchase orders, pay stubs, deposit slips, mailing labels, and tax forms. To view your forms, select Setup → Customize Forms and choose the form youd like to view. To customize forms from the view window, select Customize, make your edits, select Save Form or Save Form As, name the form, and click OK. The customized form will be saved in you Custom Forms folder. Windows Acclivity AccountEdge Pro. Mac Acclivity AccountEdge Pro. Graphics file used by Fallout 1 & 2, a role-playing video game series set in a post-apocalyptic world; stores one or more image frames referenced for gameplay; includes animal animations, speaking character heads, map objects, dialogue backgrounds, and components for the Pip-Boy interface. An image frame, which is contained in an FRM file, is an unpaletted 256-color image. Each frame has a corresponding.PAL palette file that provides color for the image or animation. The 3 starting characters in the game are pre-made and each character has a corresponding FRM,.GCD, and.BIO file. These files are all located in the premade folder. NOTE: Fallout 1 and 2 were originally developed by Interplay and Black Isle Studios but Bethesda Softworks acquired the rights. Windows Bethesda Softworks Fallout. Bethesda Softworks Fallout 2. An FRM file is a form created by ADL Software ADLForms, an application used in the real estate industry to prepare legal contracts and forms. It stores information that makes up a form, including data fields and document formatting. FRM file open in ADL Software ADLForms 6.7 ADL Software is an Australian company that develops ADLForms for real estate agents in the NSW, QLD, VIC, and WA regions. With the software, agents can create legally compliant and enforceable agreements and contracts. When you save a form with ADLForms, the app creates an FRM file to store the formatting of the document and information you have entered. After saving the form, you can close it, then re-open it to continue editing it. When you are finished editing the form you can print it or save it as a.PDF document to share it. You can only open an FRM file with ADL Software ADLForms in Windows. To open an FRM file, select File → Open. ADLForms can convert an FRM file to the Portable Document Format (PDF file) and the ADLForms Template Format (FRT file). To convert an FRM file, select File → Save as PDF or Save As Template. Windows ADL Software ADLForms. Frame stack created by Corel Painter, a digital painting application; stores a series of frames, including the width, height, resolution, and color depth of the frames; used to create animations of paintings. To create a FRM file, select File → New.. and choose the Movie With option. A Frame Stacks floating palette will appear, which can be used to navigate between the frames and to preview the animation. FRM files can be exported to QuickTime movies (.MOV files) as well as animated.GIF files. Windows Corel Painter 2022. Mac Corel Painter 2022.",
    "Windows Microsoft Visual Studio 2022. Corel WordPerfect 2021. Adobe FrameMaker. DataCAD. Windows MySQL. Aryson MySQL Database Repair. Mac MySQL. Linux MySQL. Windows Microsoft Visual Basic 6. Microsoft Visual Studio 2022. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Other text editor. Windows Acclivity AccountEdge Pro. Mac Acclivity AccountEdge Pro. Windows Bethesda Softworks Fallout. Bethesda Softworks Fallout 2. Windows ADL Software ADLForms. Windows Corel Painter 2022. Mac Corel Painter 2022.",
    "?"],
    ["developer_files",
    ".WASM",
    "WebAssembly Binary File",
    "3.9",
    "A WASM file contains binary code saved in the WebAssembly format that is run in web browsers, such as Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Microsoft Edge, and Apple Safari. It stores a module, which is binary WebAssembly code that has been compiled from C, C++, or Rust textual code, that can be imported into webpages and apps and used via JavaScript. You can compile C, C++, and Rust languages into the WebAssembly binary format (WASM file) using various programs, such as Emscripten and WebAssembly Explorer. WebAssembly is useful because it is efficient, fast, safe, and can be debugged and tested. The format also allows you to integrate open source projects written in C, C++, and Rust into webpages and apps. Windows Microsoft Edge. Google Chrome. Mozilla Firefox. Mac Apple Safari Included with OS. Google Chrome. Mozilla Firefox. Linux Google Chrome. Mozilla FirefoxFree.",
    "Windows Microsoft Edge. Google Chrome. Mozilla Firefox. Mac Apple Safari Included with OS. Google Chrome. Mozilla Firefox. Linux Google Chrome. Mozilla Firefox.",
    "?"],
    ["developer_files",
    ".BBC",
    "BBC BASIC Data File",
    "3.9",
    "BASIC program created with BBC BASIC, a development program based on the BASIC programming language; can be used to create standalone executable (.EXE) files. Windows BBC BASIC for Windows.",
    "Windows BBC BASIC for Windows.",
    "?"],
    ["developer_files",
    ".CAPX",
    "Construct Compressed Project File",
    "3.9",
    "Game development project created by Construct, a program used for making 2D games for iOS, Android, HTML5, Chrome, and other platforms; saves all project files in a compressed.ZIP format; includes graphics, sounds, physics models, and game events; used for saving and transporting the entire project as a single archive. CAPX files also include the.CAPROJ XML project file that is used as the entry point to an uncompressed project. NOTE: To save a Construct project as a CAPX file, choose File → Save As Single File.. from the application menu. Windows Scirra Construct. A CAPX file is a musical score created by Capella, a music composition program. It contains Zip-compressed, XML data that describes a scores title, notes, rests, measures, pitches, tempos, and other elements. CAPX files sometimes also include a composers comments about their score. CAPX file open in Capella 8 Capella is a Windows and Mac program that composers use to create, edit, play, and print musical scores. In Capella 7 and later versions, these scores are saved as CAPX files. CAPX files are Zip-compressed archives that contain an XML file. The XML file, which is always named score.xml, contains the data Capella uses to show and play a score. The specific XML formatting that CAPX files use, known as CapXML, is proprietary to Capella. However, CapXML is similar to the standard MusicXML (.MXL) format. Therefore, many other music composition programs can open CAPX files. NOTE: Capella scores were previously saved in the.CAP format. You can open a CAPX file in Capella (Windows, Mac), Capella Reader (Windows, Mac), or Capella Score Reader (iOS, Android). Capella Reader and Score Reader are free programs that allow composers to view, play, and print the score a CAPX or CAP file contains. Windows Capella. Capella Reader. Forte Notation. Mac Capella. Capella Reader. iOS Capella Score Reader for iOS. Android Capella Score Reader for AndroidFree.",
    "Windows Scirra Construct. Windows Capella. Capella Reader. Forte Notation. Mac Capella. Capella Reader. iOS Capella Score Reader for iOS. Android Capella Score Reader for Android.",
    "?"],
