    ".RDLC",
    "Visual Studio Client Report Definition File",
    "3.7",
    "Report definition file created by Microsoft Visual Studio, an application that allows developers to create Windows programs; contains layout settings, text fields, graphics, and other information for the report; stored using XML formatting. RDLC files are used for generating reports within a client application running Visual Studios ReportViewer control in local processing mode (in contrast to remote processing mode). Windows Microsoft Visual Studio 2022.",
