    "YML Script",
    "2.8",
    "Script written in the YML programming language; contains a list of objects in a format similar to XML, but uses brackets instead of tags; can be edited in a text editor and compiled using the yml2c compiler. YML was developed by Volker Birk and stands for Why a Markup Language?!. Mac Any text editor Windows Any text editor Linux yml2c yml2proc Any text editor.",
