    "Application interface created with Interface Builder, a graphical editor for designing and testing user interfaces; saved in a text-based flat-file format, introduced in Interface Builder 3.0. NOTE: XIB files are also called development-time format files. Previous versions of Interface Builder saved files in a deployment format with a.NIB extension. Interface Builder 3 and later (included with Apple Xcode) can save files in both the XIB and NIB formats. Mac Apple Interface Builder.",
