    "2.0",
    "File used by Cricket Audio, a software toolkit used for adding audio to games and other apps; specifies the input audio (e.g.,.WAV) files to be used when building a.CKB audio bank, which is the file used by the resulting game. You can build a CKB file from a CKBX file using the cktool program included with Cricket Audio. Windows Cricket Audio.",
    "Windows Cricket Audio.",
